{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 2782 days after the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D11"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the dexamethasone sodium phosphate shortage on 2019-02-08 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E26"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage lists five manufacturers including Eugia US LLC, Fresenius Kabi USA LLC, Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc., Mylan Institutional, and Somerset Therapeutics LLC.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E22", "E23", "E24", "E25"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Eugia Pharma Specialities Limited, the registered plant for Eugia US LLC, received an OAI classification letter dated 2026-09-21, which is 2782 days after the initial shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D11", "E19"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier inspections of the same plant in 2016, 2018, and 2018 were classified VAI, occurring 875, 353, and 56 days before the shortage posting respectively.",
      "cites": ["D8", "D9", "D10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 36 tablets of 1 mg dexamethasone with 5.5 days on hand, while Corvale General holds 169 tablets with 25.9 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 56 tablets of 1 mg from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would give Corvale East 14 days of supply while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D13"]
    }
  ]
}
